 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "s0",
   "title": "The ideal engine",
   "text": "The **Carnot engine** is the best possible engine working between a hot reservoir at \\( T_h \\) and a cold one at \\( T_c \\). Its gas goes round a cycle of **four reversible steps**: two isotherms and two adiabats.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "Th": 500,
      "Tc": 300,
      "ph": 0
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "title": "A → B: isothermal expansion",
   "text": "The gas sits on the **hot reservoir** and expands slowly. It stays at \\( T_h \\) and **absorbs heat** \\( Q_h \\), all of which becomes work (\\( \\Delta U = 0 \\)).",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "Th": 500,
      "Tc": 300,
      "ph": 0
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "ph": 0.995
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 4200
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "title": "B → C: adiabatic expansion",
   "text": "The gas is moved onto an **insulator** and keeps expanding. No heat enters, so it does work using its own energy and **cools** from \\( T_h \\) to \\( T_c \\).",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "Th": 500,
      "Tc": 300,
      "ph": 1
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "ph": 1.995
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 4200
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "title": "C → D: isothermal compression",
   "text": "On the **cold reservoir** the gas is compressed slowly at \\( T_c \\). Work is done on it, and it **rejects heat** \\( Q_c \\) to the cold reservoir.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "Th": 500,
      "Tc": 300,
      "ph": 2
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "ph": 2.995
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 4200
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "title": "D → A: adiabatic compression",
   "text": "Back on the insulator the gas is compressed further. No heat leaves, so it **warms up** from \\( T_c \\) to \\( T_h \\) and is back at A, ready to repeat.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "Th": 500,
      "Tc": 300,
      "ph": 3
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "ph": 3.995
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 4200
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s5",
   "title": "The loop is the net work",
   "text": "The **area inside the loop** ABCD is the net work per cycle: \\( W = Q_h - Q_c = {{W|0}} \\) units. The efficiency is \\( \\eta = 1 - T_c/T_h = {{eta|0}}\\% \\). Press play on **Cycle** to run it.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "Th": 500,
      "Tc": 300,
      "ph": 0
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s6",
   "title": "Only temperatures matter",
   "text": "The Carnot efficiency depends **only** on the two reservoir temperatures. Raise \\( T_h \\) or lower \\( T_c \\) to improve it. No real engine can beat it: it sets the limit.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "Th": 400,
      "Tc": 300,
      "ph": 0
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "Th": 500
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 2400
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
